            <div xml:id="d312">

                <pb facs="0451" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.5151/329: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-18T15:00:00-04:00">June 18, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. My telegram No. 56, June 13, 3 [<hi rendition="#italic">6</hi>] p.m.<anchor
                        n="43" xml:id="d312-f1"/> Entry of motor vehicles and radios in customs and
                    in transit being facilitated but Board of Exchange Control states that such
                    permits will be furnished only as conditions permit. Indications are that this
                    delay will be a question of months.</p>
                <p>Will request Minister of Foreign Affairs to endeavor to have this delay shortened
                    as much as possible in order that additional frozen credits may be obviated.</p>
                <p>Please inform Department of Commerce.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
